---
import XPWindow from './ui/XPWindow.astro';
import BadtzMaru from './ui/BadtzMaru.astro';
---

<section id="about" class="py-12 sm:py-16 scroll-mt-16">
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-4">
      <div class="space-y-1">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-(--color-text-primary)"
          style="font-family: var(--font-heading);"
        >
          About Me
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-(--color-text-secondary)">A bit about my background and what drives my engineering work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hidden sm:block pb-1" title="Badtz-Maru mascot">
        <BadtzMaru size={56} />
      </div>
    </div>

    <XPWindow title="about_ethan.txt - Notepad" icon="📝" menuBar={true}>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-(--color-text-primary) text-base max-w-none leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          I'm a final-year Computer Science student at the University of Nottingham, on track for a First, returning from a 13-month placement at Siemens Digital Industries Software in Milton Keynes. There I worked on the Simcenter FLOMASTER product team as a full-stack engineer: shipping features across WPF/MVVM interfaces, C# simulation logic, SQL Server stored procedures, and NuGet packages across seven repositories. I also automated the end-to-end delivery of SDK documentation (migrating legacy CHM files to browser-based HTML via Azure DevOps pipelines), maintained and expanded test suites across unit, integration, regression, and UI levels, diagnosed a critical VM regression traced to a SQL Server incompatibility, and mentored incoming interns.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before the placement, I worked as backend developer on a Capital One-sponsored university project, designing AWS DynamoDB schemas and mock REST APIs for a Customer Communication Channel with GDPR compliance built in from the start. My other projects cover a fair bit of ground: a kernel simulator and TCP/IP routing server in C, a machine learning project predicting forest fire burn areas, a full-stack vehicle management system with Playwright end-to-end tests, and a hackathon project that won 'Best Use of Google Gemini API' at LeedsHack 2026.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside of work I compete in powerlifting, play poker and chess, and have a music taste that goes from game soundtracks and jazz to heavy rock depending on the day. I'm looking for 2027 graduate roles where the codebase is genuinely interesting and the team cares about getting it right.
        </p>
      </div>
    </XPWindow>
  </div>
</section>
